       "title": "Read-only public status and owner-authenticated config control",
-      "statement": "Given the dashboard's public surface, when any caller reads current cycle stage, next scheduled run, recent cycle outcomes, cumulative distributed total, holder count, a disclosed degraded or quarantined balance, or held positions, then no response requires authentication or mutates state. The held-position projection exposes only count plus each position's reason class, age, and cycle state; it never exposes signer identity, exact holder balance, card reference, memo, mint, evidence digest, or in-flight authorization digest. Given the owner surface, when the owner reads or writes interval, pack codes, pause state, spend cap, held-position count and value limits, or unresolved-card deadline through a timing-safe-compared bearer credential, then the write is schema-validated and never itself moves funds, signs, or broadcasts. The owner view shows each position, its cycle, reason, age, value, decision state, and limit usage, and sends a digest- and position-revision-bound sell or keep-holding decision. Edge case: kicking a stuck cycle (`supersede`) and the distribution-signer/verifier approval are never dashboard buttons; both require an out-of-band signature the dashboard can only surface as a status line, never trigger.",
