-      "statement": "Given a planned cycle, when the runner executes it, then its ordered stages are eligibility-snapshot, claim-process, outbound, purchase, open, epic-gate, buyback, return, and payout. The runner persists the immutable cycle mode before stage execution and production services refuse rehearsal cycles while rehearsal services refuse production cycles. Before signing a purchase, it persists typed {chainId, assetId, decimals, amountAtomic} values for unitPriceAtomic, totalAtomic, and boundedOverheadAtomic plus positive integer-string quantity; totalAtomic equals quantity multiplied by unitPriceAtomic, all money fields share the same asset identity, and policy reserves totalAtomic plus boundedOverheadAtomic. A card carved into a held position no longer keeps the cycle terminally held. Return and the main payout bridge and distribute only settled, cycle-attributed proceeds, list excluded positions in their evidence, and allow COMPLETED with open positions or a zero-proceeds, zero-manifest COMPLETED result when every card is held. A completed record with open positions remains one active DurableCycleStore entry for supplementary recovery even though scheduler admission skips it. The 16-entry store supports the default `maxHeldPositions` 10 when positions span completed cycles; a configuration above that verified-safe value of 10 is refused at admission until post-completion position archival or a measured store-capacity exemption exists. Outbound can use only the cycle's claimed principal. No bucket can fund another cycle. The custody ledger records finalized observed current balances separately from obligations, counts unresolved principal exactly once, records expected cycle assets separately from unattributed external deposits, and pauses new claims for those deposits. For the canonical EVM native ETH row only, hookemon.custody-ledger.v3 with an independently finalized native balance observation carries a verifiedCurrentBalance (CustodyBalanceObservationV1 | null) and a singular expectedCycleAsset (TypedAmount | null, never a collection), and unvaluedExposure becomes true whenever verifiedCurrentBalance is null while unresolved principal is positive or any current-custody bucket is nonzero. A pure, two-independent-source finalized-observation combiner (packages/adapters/src/solana-custody-balance-observation.mjs#combineFinalizedBalanceObservation and #observeFinalizedBalanceWithRetry) is an allowed evidence-construction contract for a future non-EVM verifiedCurrentBalance; it is not itself a durable producer, a canonical chain/asset identity source, a custody-ledger writer, a valuation, or live readiness proof, and constructing its output does not by itself satisfy this requirement. Any non-native-EVM row stays on hookemon.custody-ledger.v1, or, if migrated to v2, stays permanently unvalued and fail-closed under the same admission rule until a separately approved evidence producer exists for it. Native principal and gas share the ETH asset identity but occupy separate reservation and cost buckets; spendable principal excludes the gas reserve and unpaid obligations. Only finalized cycle-attributed native payment proofs may become an Operations ETH credit or payout basis. A direct native payment is proved from the persisted signed transaction identity, exact sender, recipient, value and calldata, successful receipt and canonical finalized block; a trusted hook post-payment event proves a claim. Internal Relay return or refund proof additionally authenticates emitter runtime, request linkage, decoded recipient/value and failure propagation. Missing proof leaves proceeds unavailable. No wallet-wide delta or fabricated ERC20 Transfer event proves a native credit. Historical USDG journals remain readable but cannot resume through the native runtime or be rescaled; native cycles use fresh identities. Edge case: an unattributed inbound deposit, cross-mode request, mismatched purchase total, bridge-funded cross-cycle action, a non-native-EVM v2 row treated as valued without an approved producer, or attempt to finance one cycle with another fails closed.",
