ionV1 | null) and a singular expectedCycleAsset (TypedAmount | null, never a collection), and unvaluedExposure becomes true whenever verifiedCurrentBalance is null while unresolved principal is positive or any current-custody bucket is nonzero. A pure, two-independent-source finalized-observation combiner (packages/adapters/src/solana-custody-balance-observation.mjs#combineFinalizedBalanceObservation and #observeFinalizedBalanceWithRetry) is an allowed evidence-construction contract for a future non-EVM verifiedCurrentBalance; it is not itself a durable producer, a canonical chain/asset identity source, a custody-ledger writer, a valuation, or live readiness proof, and constructing its output does not by itself satisfy this requirement. Any non-native-EVM row stays on hookemon.custody-ledger.v1, or, if migrated to v2, stays permanently unvalued and fail-closed under the same admission rule until a separately approved evidence producer exists for it. Native principal and gas share the ETH asset identity but occupy separate reservation and cost buckets; spendable principal excludes the gas reserve and unpaid obligations. Only finalized cycle-attributed native payment proofs may become an Operations ETH credit or payout basis. A direct native payment is proved from the persisted signed transaction identity, exact sender, recipient, value and calldata, successful receipt and canonical finalized block; a trusted hook post-payment event proves a claim. Internal Relay return or refund proof additionally authenticates emitter runtime, request linkage, decoded recipient/value and failure propagation. Missing proof leaves proceeds unavailable. No wallet-wide delta or fabricated ERC20 Transfer event proves a native credit. Historical USDG journals remain readable but cannot resume through the native runtime or be rescaled; native cycles use fresh identities. Edge case: an unattributed inbound deposit, cross-mode request, mismatched purchase total, bridge-funded cross-cycle action, a non-native-EVM v2 row treated as valued without an approved producer, or attempt to finance one cycle with another fails closed. New native cycles atomically persist a versioned rewardSelection snapshot in cycle-opened, binding cycleId, configurationRevision, rewardRecipientLimit and a canonical domain-separated digest. Resume reads only that snapshot; later configuration edits cannot change it. Existing native cycle-opened records without this field remain on the historical all-holder path without mutation or digest changes. Supplementary payouts retain the original cycle selection.",
+      "measurement": "End-to-end fakes and fork tests assert exact nine-stage order, typed-amount validation, purchase arithmetic and reserve, immutable mode isolation, held-position carve-out, settled-proceeds-only return and payout, all-held zero completion, completed-record supplementary recovery without reopening the main cycle, interleaved-cycle isolation, asset separation, cycle-attribution keys, claimed-principal-only outbound, proceeds-delta-only return, finality before completion, observed-balance and obligation conservation, one-time unresolved-principal accounting, pause on unattributed deposits, and independent gas reserves; custody-ledger fixtures additionally prove the EVM native ETH row's unvaluedExposure admission rule on a null verifiedCurrentBalance with nonzero unresolved claim or current-custody bucket, the singular non-collection expectedCycleAsset write-time refusal of a second unresolved return leg, and that a non-native-EVM row constructed as v2 remains permanently unvalued absent an approved producer. Native tests reject wrong request/emitter/runtime/value, failed internal calls, unrelated deposits, stale or reorged receipts, duplicate proofs, old USDG resume and any principal spending that consumes the gas reserve. Test atomic opening, policy digest tampering, changed operator settings before and after restart, historic absent-field replay, cross-cycle policy substitution and supplementary reuse of the original selection.",
