       "id": "REQ-eligibility-snapshot-1",
       "kind": "security",
       "title": "Pre-claim finalized eligibility snapshot",
-      "statement": "Given a planned cycle, when eligibility-snapshot runs as the first cycle stage, then before claimProcess the runner pins a finalized block and hash, replays HKMN Transfer logs from deployment through that block, reconciles mint minus burn against the launch manifest, rechecks the block hash after scanning, and proves log completeness through an independent second source or archive RPC. It excludes zero and burn addresses, Hook, PoolManager, custody, Operations, Treasury, Programmable, launch contracts, and historical role holders while allowing contract holders to receive native ETH at their own addresses, with bounded native payout simulation before claim. It evaluates recipient count, measured gas, gas-price cap, native balance, and transaction count before claim. Edge case: a reorg, incomplete or unordered logs, supply mismatch, missing source, or infeasible payout envelope prevents the claim.",
-      "measurement": "Snapshot tests inject each log and reorg fault, compare deterministic manifests, prove supply reconciliation and hash recheck, and assert no claim request is prepared before the feasibility envelope passes.",
+      "statement": "Given a planned cycle, when eligibility-snapshot runs as the first cycle stage, then before claimProcess the runner pins a finalized block and hash, replays HKMN Transfer logs from deployment through that block, reconciles mint minus burn against the launch manifest, rechecks the block hash after scanning, and proves log completeness through an independent second source or archive RPC. It excludes zero and burn addresses, Hook, PoolManager, custody, Operations, Treasury, Programmable, launch contracts, and historical role holders while allowing contract holders to receive native ETH at their own addresses, with bounded native payout simulation before claim. It evaluates recipient count, measured gas, gas-price cap, native balance, and transaction count before claim. Edge case: a reorg, incomplete or unordered logs, supply mismatch, missing source, or infeasible payout envelope prevents the claim. For cycles with an explicit rewardSelection snapshot, selection follows complete verified holder replay and exclusions: rank positive direct HKMN balances descending, break ties by normalized address ascending, and retain at most rewardRecipientLimit holders. Persist selected entries in canonical address order, configured limit and actual selectedCount separately, and enough full-holder evidence to reconstruct ranking and supply reconciliation. The allocation denominator is the sum of selected balances; excluded and unselected balances are excluded from that denominator but remain in full-supply evidence. Evaluate native recipient, transaction and gas feasibility against the selected set; never silently reduce the chosen set to make an infeasible envelope pass. Cycles without the snapshot keep the historical all-holder semantics.",
+      "measurement": "Snapshot tests inject each log and reorg fault, compare deterministic manifests, prove supply reconciliation and hash recheck, and assert no claim request is prepared before the feasibility envelope passes. Cover excess, fewer, absent, excluded, tied and zero-weight holders; reproduce selection and selection evidence digests independently; reject count, policy, holder evidence and supply mismatch. Preserve full replay evidence and prove selected plus unselected plus excluded balances equals supply.",
       "module": "eligibility-snapshot",
       "status": "approved"
     },
@@ -680,8 +680,8 @@
       "id": "REQ-direct-payout-1",
       "kind": "security",
       "title": "Finalized direct holder payout",
-      "statement": "Given a finalized cycle-attributed Operations native ETH credit and its frozen eligibility manifest, when the main payout begins, then the runner sends direct native ETH value payments only for settled cards through the durable chain-attempt contract: PREPARED(requestDigest, policyDigest, fencingToken), SIGNED(rawSignedBytesHash, nonceOrBlockhash, txHash, approvedSemanticsDigest), BROADCAST, FINALIZED, or REFUSED(reason, fencingToken). The first accepted sell decision for one held position atomically creates exactly one supplementary settlement keyed by that position's ID, starting a supplementary buyback, return leg for only that position's attributed proceeds, and supplementary payout with manifest ID `<cycleId>:supplementary:<n>`; an exact replay of that same sell request returns the identical settlement and manifest identifier, a conflicting or later sell request for an already-settled or in-flight position fails, and a resolved position can never create a second manifest. The settlement persists the digest of the original completed eligibility snapshot; its RETURN_BROADCAST boundary persists the exact finalized return and return binding as a payout-source digest, and binds that return and any permitted dust source to a one-time atomic consumption record shared across every supplementary manifest for that position, so at most one supplementary manifest is ever funded per held position and per return source. The supplementary payout accepts only that snapshot and source, becomes immutable at its first broadcast, and pays every recipient exactly once for that manifest. It uses zero/null dust unless that same atomic position-aware supplementary dust-consumption transition has bound an unconsumed original-cycle source. The wallet-wide nonce lock covers claim, outbound, return, main payout, and supplementary payout. SIGNED records retain immutable retrievable signed bytes and recover after restart. A dropped BROADCAST resolves by receipt search or a replacement using the same nonce and calldata, after revalidating the persisted approvedSemanticsDigest. It marks paid only after proof of the exact successful finalized transaction matched to persisted signed bytes/hash, source, recipient, value and calldata; a recipient may forward ETH and its ending balance is not payment proof. Rejected recipient calls become quarantine liabilities without blocking the rest of a manifest; dust carry is durable and atomically consumed and written between cycles. Edge case: a crash between supplementary broadcast and finality, duplicate recipient, nonce collision, replacement with different calldata, changed approval digest, dropped broadcast, rejecting recipient, or dust replay cannot create a double payment or silently change either manifest.",
